Text Variables - Introduction
1. Word Counts:
    Count total words in a text column
    Use: detect verbosity, short vs long entries, missing text

2. Token Frequency
    Break text into tokens (words) and count frequency across the dataset
    Helps identify common terms, medical jargon, or repeated notes

3. Basic Pattern Recognition
    Detect specific keywords, phrases, or patterns (eg "urgent", "biopsy")
    Useful for flagging important cases

Why this Matters?
    Even simple text analysis can reveal hidden signals in medical datasets (e.g., doctors’ notes, patient reports).
    Word counts → measure verbosity.
    Token frequency → highlight common terms.
    Pattern recognition → flag critical cases.